@startuml glance_focus_states
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' glance_focus_states — the glance panel after design A (v22.4).
' Converted from Mermaid in the v26.8 audit (indexed, never rendered).
'
' The whole point: FOUR visible shapes and ZERO stored mode. Every state is
' derived on refresh(now) from two booleans. A stored "panelMode" field would
' have been the obvious design and would have rotted the first time a task
' was planned from a different page — the stored mode would have said Focus
' while the truth said Clear. Derive, don't store (design-doc §3.5).
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

title The glance panel — four shapes, no stored mode

state "Derive\nrefresh(now)\nlist = tasksNeedingBlock(...)\nlooked = nextReturn(lastReview) > now" as derive

state "HIDDEN\ncard hidden entirely\npanel is what it always was" as hidden
state "CLEAR\n«Everything's on the calendar»\nput-off strip only" as clear
state "FOCUS\nGATE — card takes the panel's stretch\nONE task, hero density\n«1 of N» expands to the list" as focus
state "STRIP\nreviewed — day content returns\npinned rows stay visible\ncard sizes to its content" as strip

[*] --> derive

derive --> hidden : list empty\nand none put off
derive --> clear  : list empty\nbut some put off
derive --> focus  : list non-empty\nand not looked
derive --> strip  : list non-empty\nand looked

focus --> strip : «Show my day»\n(writes lastReview)
strip --> focus : nextReturn passes\n(re-arms at 06:00)
focus --> clear : last task planned
strip --> hidden : nothing left at all

note right of focus
  The gate is a <b>stretch factor</b>, not a
  fixed height: the card CLAIMS the panel's
  space rather than asking for it. See
  needsblock_height_bound for why that
  distinction cost a release to learn.
end note
@enduml
